Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

D679/D680. When a debrief is answered „helped" on a relayed ask, the asker's
goal conversation gets one card: „shall I thank Zurab for you?" — yes / no
need. On yes, Zurab's own conversation gets one fixed line in his language,
„Nino says thank you for your help.", rung once (push quiet hours apply). On
either answer, one private tap follows: „would you ask Zurab again?" — stored
as helper_thanks.ask_again for the answer record (A6), never shown.

Migration 227 adds helper_thanks (one row per answered ask: share_result,
result_line, ask_again, the times). All text is the server's; none of the
asker's typed words goes to the helper.

Part 2, not here: the „yes, and tell him the result" option with the result in
the assistant's own words (model text, D44), the bridges of a chain, the
day-7 re-ask and day-14 „following up your lead" line, and counting the
thank-you against the 4-a-day relayed cap.

